  "repo_truth": "The parent submits an immutable 47-path HCM-2.3 post-remediation implementation subject. Review 1 returned actionable findings; the parent changed the subject, reran focused, HCM-2.2, cross-platform, package, validator, and complete workspace proof, and records no CLEAN conclusion. The candidate control classifications remain conditional on this different-fresh review and primary commit.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Remain read-only and replay all 47 manifest hashes, ordinal ordering, aggregate fingerprint, active-dispatch exclusion, dispatch schema, selected handoff, and branch/HEAD authority before review.",
    "Independently review every production, test, fixture, control-pack, prior dispatch, and proof path in the immutable subject against the complete HCM-2.3 packet and runtime contracts.",
    "Review correctness, readability/simplicity, architecture, security, performance, dependency discipline, source-kind schema containment, recovered authority and lock order, native safe repository I/O, persistence/recovery, idempotency, and CLI exit/output behavior.",
    "Return evidence-backed findings ordered Critical, Required, Optional, Nit with exact file/line evidence, failure mode, smallest authority-preserving repair, and missing validation."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, branch changes, preservation/archive access, or user task hops.",
    "No HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, Phase 4 SDK/transport, package-default expansion, resolver redesign, built-in namespace expansion, or HCM-2.2 reinterpretation.",
    "Do not accept passing tests or the proof narrative as a success conclusion; verify implementation and tests independently."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Invoke the required skills, read repository AGENTS.md and the complete dispatch, and return BLOCKED on any manifest, branch, HEAD, handoff, or authority mismatch.",
    "Review tests first and map every mandatory HCM-2.3 and explicitly authorized schema-root behavior to an effective regression that would fail for the wrong implementation.",
    "Audit fixed BuiltIn definitions/schemas containment and allowlist-only bytes; request-root-only Repository containment; cache and error precedence; the sole HCM-2.3 request root; and unchanged high-level schema resolver.",
    "Audit recovery-first authority retention and revalidation across ordinary reads, replay lookup, planning, establishment, canonical replacement, and generic lock ordering.",
    "Audit component substitution, symlink, hard-link, non-regular, same-size/time mutation, traversal, descriptor/handle retention, inventory bounds, create-new, rename, remove, durability, and cross-platform behavior.",
    "Audit BuiltIn intake compatibility, repository intake meta-validation, blocked provenance, structural preview validation, dynamic value closure, refusal tuples, exact journal descriptors, ledger/tombstone closure, time sampling, and family fsync.",
    "Audit exact selection closure, generic operation context, canonical YAML, pure intake evaluation, immutable lineage, crash recovery, idempotency retention, zero-write validation, compare-and-write promotion, concurrency, and all HCM-2.2 preservation.",
    "Audit the actual CLI boundary for ten fixed commands, explicit authority, stable exits, JSON/human rendering, path/stdin handling, no direct writes, no raw-key disclosure, and no per-kind/example dispatch.",
    "Verify control-pack language remains review-pending/candidate-only, broader gates stay open, and no package definition, Cargo/dependency, HCM-2.2, HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, SDK/transport, archive, or preservation path changed.",
    "Return CLEAN only with zero Critical, Required, Optional, and Nit findings; otherwise return CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repairing files."
  ],
